--TEST--
A control character XML cannot write is refused written literally, in text, an attribute, a comment, an instruction and a CDATA section, by the tree and the stream alike, as its reference already was — `rule:core-classes/xml-tree-and-stream`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Each document carries one character no XML document may hold. A tree that
// kept one could not be written back out by its own `source`.
array<string> $documents = [
    "<a>x\0y</a>",
    "<a b=\"x\x01y\"/>",
    "<a><!--x\x01y--></a>",
    "<a><?go x\x01y?></a>",
    "<a><![CDATA[x\x1Fy]]></a>",
];
foreach ($documents as string $document) {
    try {
        Core\Xml::parse($document);
        echo "parsed\n";
    } catch (ParseError $tree) {
        echo $tree->message, "\n";
    }
}

// The stream reaches the same refusal at the node that carries it.
Core\Xml\Reader $reader = Core\Xml::reader("<a><b/>x\x01y</a>");
try {
    while ($reader->read() != null) {
        echo "node at depth ", $reader->depth(), "\n";
    }
} catch (ParseError $stream) {
    echo $stream->message, "\n";
}

// The three whitespace control characters are XML, and are kept.
Core\Xml\Node $kept = Core\Xml::parse("<a b=\"\t\">x\ty</a>");
foreach ($kept->children() as Core\Xml\Node $root) {
    echo Core\Str::length($root->attributes()["b"]), " ", Core\Str::length($root->source()), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Xml::parse(): the document holds U+0000, which XML does not allow.
Core\Xml::parse(): the document holds U+0001, which XML does not allow.
Core\Xml::parse(): the document holds U+0001, which XML does not allow.
Core\Xml::parse(): the document holds U+0001, which XML does not allow.
Core\Xml::parse(): the document holds U+001F, which XML does not allow.
node at depth 0
node at depth 1
Core\Xml\Reader::read(): the document holds U+0001, which XML does not allow.
1 19
